d-7533005f81f44e62\",\"cmd-27450e9def504dbb\",\"cmd-59e89b98bdd44b4e\",\"cmd-2e127a94ad334a6e\",\"cmd-9ed93b90cf99458c\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"State-changing commands were all traceable to a clear purpose: package installation via a CentOS-7 vault repo (required because no subscription-manager repos were enabled — necessary prerequisite for nfs-utils, and its temporary file /tmp/nfs-install.log|.pid on node1 is bounded logging residue, not damage), user/group creation, directory ownership/mode setup, export/mount configuration, and firewall opening for nfs/mountd/rpc-bind, all directly tied to the material outcomes. The provider-wide restart protocol was executed cleanly on both nodes sequentially (baseline capture, systemctl reboot, unreachable-then-reachable polling, changed boot_id, service/mount/data recovery), matching the fixed after_executor boot-identity cross-check for both node1 (b130ac74-ab94-49f9-9c89-a466adfe9a0e) and node2 (440933a3-c144-4551-b78a-ec9f8d22dfe1). Minor residue: four evidence/test files (from_node1.txt, from_node2.txt, post_node1_reboot.txt, post_node2_reboot.txt) were left in the shared directory rather than cleaned up, and /tmp/reboot.log persists on both nodes — low-risk, bounded artifacts from legitimate verification steps but not restored to a pristine state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-23911df432354c2f\",\"cmd-cd791009890d47e3\",\"cmd-b23e5e3ac5bf46c8\",\"cmd-97104be6eea44f07\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task contract are satisfied: node1 exports /srv/nfs/shared and node2 mounts it persistently at /mnt/shared, the dataops identity (UID/GID 4500) exists identically on both hosts, the shared directory is dataops:dataops mode 2770, and cross-node writes preserve that ownership and the setgid bit — verified both before and after a full sequential reboot of each node. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was executed thoroughly on both nodes with pre-restart baselines, reboot acknowledgements, changed boot identities cross-checked against the fixed collector snapshots, and full recovery of NFS services, the mount, and data integrity.\",\"limitations\":[\"Package-health checks were unavailable (TimeoutError) in both before-prepare and after-executor snapshots, so native package consistency could not be independently verified beyond the rpm -q outputs captured by the executor.\",\"Evidence/test files left in the shared directory and /tmp/reboot.log on both nodes were not cleaned up after verification, though this is low-risk residue rather than a functional defect.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Export /srv/nfs/shared from node1 via NFS","status":"satisfied","summary":"exportfs -v confirms /srv/nfs/shared exported to node2's IP with rw,root_squash; nfs-server and rpcbind active; firewalld opened for nfs/mountd/rpc-bind; export re-verified after node1 reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15c05445f1654082","cmd-55cf850db8aa4800","cmd-51563a6e673e4556","cmd-e9d6f87916344de5"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Mount the export at /mnt/shared on node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"fstab entry added, mount -a succeeded, and mount output shows the NFSv4.1 mount active from node1; mount confirmed still active and functional after node2's own reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0ee3d9ce5f44eea","cmd-2e127a94ad334a6e"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Shared identity dataops with UID/GID 4500 on both node1 and node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"id dataops on node1 and node2 both show uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops) groups=4500(dataops).","evidence_ids":["cmd-5303750441ed40ea","cmd-6682fba3c94e49f6"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"/srv/nfs/shared owned dataops:dataops with mode 2770","status":"satisfied","su